From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: npu: advance the RX ring past an unfinished descriptor

mt76_npu_dequeue() walks up to NPU_RX_DMA_PKT_COUNT_MASK descriptors of one
NPU RX frame.  When a descriptor's NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE bit is still clear it
frees the skb built so far and returns NULL, but q->tail and q->queued are
only assigned after the loop.  Nothing in the driver ever clears that DONE
bit either, so the next mt76_npu_rx_poll() re-reads the very same descriptor,
rebuilds a skb on top of the page_pool buffer that the freed skb already
returned, and frees it a second time.

Stopping the walk is enough.  The descriptors that are not done yet have not
been consumed, the ones that are already done stay where they are, and
q->tail/q->queued move forward by exactly the number of frames taken.  The
NPU raises the RX interrupt again for the remainder.

Break out of the loop so the unified exit publishes the progress made.  The
dev_kfree_skb() goes away with the early return: skb is still handed to the
caller when at least one descriptor was ready, and NULL when none was.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---
 npu.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -75,10 +75,8 @@
 		int len = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_CUR_LEN_MASK,
 				    desc[index].ctrl);
 
-		if (!FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[index].ctrl)) {
-			dev_kfree_skb(skb);
-			return NULL;
-		}
+		if (!FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[index].ctrl))
+			break;
 
 		dma_sync_single_for_cpu(dev->dma_dev, e->dma_addr[0],
 					e->dma_len[0],
